    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21720" root="شجب" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجَبٌ</span></b>  <i>Grief,</i> or <i>sorrow;</i> and <i>anxiety:</i> (K,
TA:) but the word more commonly known is
with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ن</span> [i.e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجَنٌ</span>]. (TA.) [The pl. is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْجَابٌ</span>
(like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْجَانٌ</span>) occurring in the O, See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجِبَ</span>,
of which it is the inf. n.: and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجْبٌ</span>, first

sentence.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>Distress that befalls a man by
reason of disease</i> or <i>of fight.</i> (K, * TA.)

